===Etymology===
{{etymon|en|:clip|radiotelegraphy}}
Short for {{m|en|radiotelegraphy}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈɹeɪ.diˌəʊ/|a=RP}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˈɹeɪ.diˌoʊ/|a=GA}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-radio.ogg|a=US}}
* {{hyph|en|ra|dio}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{senseid|en|Q872}}{{lb|en|uncountable}} The [[technology]] that allows for the [[transmission]] of sound or other signals by [[modulation]] of [[electromagnetic wave]]s.
#: {{ux|en|send a message by '''radio'''}}
# {{senseid|en|Q159391}}{{lb|en|countable}} A device that can capture (receive) the signal sent over radio waves and render the modulated signal as [[sound]].
#: {{co|en|''(of a song, person, etc.)'' to be <u>on</u> the '''radio'''}}
#: {{co|en|''(of a song, etc.)'' to play on/be played on/get played on/come on the '''radio'''}}
#: {{ux|en|We heard the news over the '''radio'''.}}
#: {{ux|en|We heard a lovely song on the '''radio'''.}}
#: {{ux|en| She was listening to the '''radio''' when he knocked on the door.}}
## {{lb|en|countable|by extension}} Any audio playing device, such as the on-board entertainment system in a car, usually including a radio receiver as well as the capability to play audio from recorded media; see also '''''[[car radio]]'''''.
#* {{quote-web|en|author=Jonathan Amos|title=Elon Musk's huge Falcon Heavy rocket set for launch|work=BBC News|url=http://www.bbc.co.uk/news/science-environment-42950957|location=London, United Kingdom|publisher=BBC|date=2018-02-06|accessdate=2018-02-07|passage=David Bowie's classic hit Space Oddity will be looping on the '''radio''' as the car is hurled into an elliptical orbit that stretches out to Mars' orbit around the Sun.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20260905144851/https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/science-environment-42950957|archivedate=5 September 2026}}
# {{lb|en|countable}} A device that can transmit radio signals.
# {{lb|en|Internet|uncountable}} The continuous [[broadcast]]ing of [[sound]] via the [[Internet]] in the style of traditional radio.

